{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"59fe4dca5575425a","name":"card_event_air_land_sea","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/CovertOp/events/card_event_air_land_sea","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"AIR, LAND & SEA","text":"Develop a card in your deck. Lose a kredit slot.","flavorText":"During WWII, Japan's military strategy was heavily reliant on its capabilities in the air, on land, and at sea. In the air, the Imperial Japanese Navy Air Service (IJNAS) and Imperial Japanese Army Air Service (IJAAS) were initially powerful, achieving surprise attacks like Pearl Harbor and early victories in the Pacific. However, their aircraft, pilot training programs and manufacturing capabilities couldn't keep pace with the Allies and this led to their decline. On land, the Imperial Japanese Army (IJA) was known for its brutal tactics and initial successes in conquering territories in Southeast Asia and the Pacific. However, its overextended supply lines, the logistical challenges it faced, and the relentless attacks of Allied forces led to its eventual defeat.. At sea, the Imperial Japanese Navy (IJN) was a powerful force, with a focus on aircraft carriers and innovative tactics. Early victories such as in the Indian Ocean Raid boosted their confidence, but their losses in crucial battles like the Battle of Midway and the Battle of the Philippine Sea turned the tide against them. Despite their initial successes, Japan's overconfidence, resource limitations, and strategic miscalculations ultimately led to their defeat in all three domains.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["ability.develop"],"Name":"card_event_air_land_sea","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_air_land_sea_title","SourceString":"AIR, LAND & SEA","LocalizedString":"AIR, LAND & SEA"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":1